  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Deleting friend requests seems like it's not working properly on both ends. In the event that a user sends another user a friend request, and the sender cancels the friend request, the recipient will receive a message from the websocket to remove the notification from the UI, but refreshing the page will make it come back when it asks the API for the current set of notifications. Also the “Cancel Friend Request” button on the senders end will never go away. \n\nIf the recipient of the notification declines the friend request, then the notification will actually delete, but the API will still treat viewing each other’s profile as if the friend request still exists, as “outgoingRequest” is still returning true for the sender, and “incomingRequest” is still returning true for the recipient from the friendStatus endpoint. The only way I can see to exit this state is if the recipient visits the sender’s profile, and clicks “Accept Friend Request”, where the users will now be friends despite the friend request being deleted.",
